    "done_when": "1. reckon/crew/ticker.py:row_moment and its _NAMED_ZONE guard, and reckon/_backends.py's _CACHED_STAMP_ZONE guard near :762. Both decide whether a stamp names a zone from the text's shape, so the offset spellings fromisoformat accepts (+00, -05, +000000) read as no zone. ticker then reads the stamp as local wall-clock time, a 7200 s shift under TZ=Europe/Paris for -05; _backends returns None for the cache stamp. Both now read a stated zone from reckon._timestamps.parse_iso's tzinfo, and the regex guards are deleted. For those spellings, each returns the output base cea6da07 returned.\n2. reckon/_store.py:write_json_atomically. A failure of os.fdopen after the chmod leaves the sibling created by os.open on disk. Every failure after the temporary exists now removes it.\n3. write_json_atomically gains an ensure_ascii keyword defaulting to today's True. reckon/hooks/install.py:_write_settings passes ensure_ascii=False, so a non-ASCII hook-script path is written literally, as it was before the second writer wave.\n\ntests/test_zone_guards_read_tzinfo.py records at base 92274925, by running the base code:\n- row_moment under TZ=Europe/Paris for +00, -05 and +000000;\n- the _backends cache-stamp reader for the same spellings;\n- the settings bytes for a non-ASCII script path.\nIt asserts the head reproduces the base values for the zone spellings and the pre-wave literal bytes for the settings file. It also asserts that an os.fdopen patched to raise leaves no file beside the destination. The TZ environment is set with monkeypatch and time.tzset, and restored afterwards.\n\nThat file, tests/test_timestamp_callers_batch_c.py, tests/test_writer_callers_second_wave.py and tests/test_shared_helper_edges.py pass at exit 0. The manifest writes baseline_suite and after_suite each as one line of armed JSON: revision, command with no placeholder, exit_status, completed, failure_count, failure_ids, log_path. The head arm runs at the committed head, and every gate log opens with one line naming its revision, tree and command. The declared negative control is applied and observed to fail, and its log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Replace the text-shaped zone guards in ticker and _backends with parse_iso's tzinfo, close the fdopen cleanup gap in the shared writer, and let the hook installer write non-ASCII paths literally again",
